Note:  There is a big-time bug report at the end of this.  If you are
looking for those, read on.

Well, I could ascend with 3.0.  It wasn't easy, but I could do it.
With 3.1, it doesn't seem possible.

The possibility of instant death is much greater in 3.1.

Well, some of this could be interpreted as spoilers, but it's mostly
pretty mild.


I turned a corner in the Gnomish mines, and saw a Gnome lord.  As I
saw him (before I could back up or anything), he zapped a wand of
sleep.  Even though I had about 70 HP and -5 AC at the time, he calmly
walked up and hit me a few dozen times until I died.  No warning.
Nothing I can do.  Ouch.

In future patches, I expect monsters to have to take one turn to WIELD
their wands, and not to zap them unless the character is visible to
the monster.  Out of fairness, make the character wield wands before
zapping them, as well.  Seeing a monster wield the thing would give a
chance to run away!

In games after that, I carefully explore the Dungeons of Doom before
attempting the Gnomish Mines.  The presence of wands and intelligent
monsters (gnomes, mostly) makes the Mines much too dangerous.

A nymph stole my armor and weapon.  She then stole a crystal plate
mail from a shop and PUT IT ON.  Needless to say, she was rather hard
to hit after that stunt.  But wait!  The worst is yet to come.  I
started firing off arrows at her (to keep her from stealing anything
else).  She took two hits, then zapped a wand of digging and FELL
THROUGH THE HOLE!!  Needless to say, I chased her down the hole.
She repeated this trick about seven times, until I found my 5th level
samurai on level 14.  I finally snuffed a cockatrice and took her out
in a single shot with the corpse.  While chasing her around, I fell in
a pit trap and touched the corpse.  By an incredible stroke of luck, the
unidentified amulet I was wearing was an amulet of life saving.  Anyway,
she didn't get to run away any more, since she was instantly a statue.
So I get my stuff back, right?  WRONG!!!!  All of it disappeared when
she turned into a statue!!!  OUCH!!

In the next patch, I expect all monsters to drop what they are
carrying when they die, no matter how they pass from this life.

Since the monsters are using the wands, they are all used up by the
time I get to them.  Few things are more useless than a wand of fire
with no charges in it.  Ouch.

Don't put wands of cancellation in bags of holding.  Just don't.  I
found out why.  You don't want to know.  Ouch.

In the future, I expect former contents of such former bags to be blown
about the level.  I was very disappointed with what actually happened to
them.

The encumbrance is more realistic, but it has some problems.  I
finished killing a large monster (owlbear, I think) on the square
RIGHT NEXT to an aligned altar.  I picked it up and got "hardly move a
handspan" message.  No problem.  I'm right next to the altar, right?
Wrong.  As I moved ONE SPACE to the altar, a mumak came in and hit me
several times, and killed me before I could do anything.  Yet another
opportunity for instant death.  Ouch.

In the future, I expect moving while heavily encumbered to work like
eating or spellbook reading.  You can stop moving if you want, and 
start dropping things.

Given the general nastiness about the game, I find it necessary to
turn invisible as soon as possible.  Otherwise, the various nasties
tend to mob me.  This is particularly bad at the fort.  Of course,
this means that shopkeepers won't let me in.  Well, I can get in via a
wand of digging, but THAT means paying an extra few hundred $$ to fix
the walls, and only works if I can dig.  This makes shops much less
useful.  Ouch!

In the future, I expect shopkeepers to welcome all customers,
invisible or not.  They can detect invisible.  They should just be
able to sell to anyone.

I went to a temple and thought I would be clever.  I zapped the create
monster wand and sacrificed the results.  I thought I was doing a good
thing, until I realized that combat in temples is VERY offensive to
deities.  Oops.  However, monsters can still THROW while in temples.

In the future, I expect monsters to be incapable of ANY attack while
in a temple.  Also, it might be a good idea to simply make character
attacks impossible.  Then again, you couldn't attack the priest.
Maybe not.

I thought I would be clever and convert an altar in a temple.  The
priest got mad.  The priest got REAL mad.  He cast some spell and and
held me in place, then killed me.  Yep, nothing I could do about it.  I
didn't know he'd get mad (makes sense, though).  Yet another instant
death.

It would seem that magical resistance is essential to this game.  So
is reflection (shield or amulet).  Unfortunately, I have NEVER managed
to get magic resistance (outside of being a wizard).  I have only ONCE
managed to get reflection (that game had two shield and one amulet).
I have also gotten only one wish.  Given that this equipment is so
essential, there should perhaps be a side quest to gain these.

I had a game where I managed to eat four (peaceful) tengus.  I never
got teleport control.  Tengus are so rare, they should work like
floating eyes.  Eating one should always get you the intrinsic.

On balance, there ARE some good things.  A luckstone, while always
necessary, is consistently available.  You don't need to eat something
poisonous to get poison resistance.  Shops are always available.  The
Oracle is always available.  The bit with bell, book, and candle
really got me.  What's next, "Hello Sailor" and grues?  Of course, we
do already have Zorkmids.  Do talk to the Oracle.  He's very helpful
(if expensive).  The unicorn horn seems to be much more useful.  The
use of lamps adds an interesting touch.  Finally, the ability to
recover crashed games is great.

Well, one game I thought I really had it made.  My best game ever
(isn't it always?).  I made it to the bottom of the mine (although I
couldn't seem to find the item there).  I killed Medusa and went down
the stairs.  I had reflection, polymorph, and polymorph control.  I
had -17 AC as a vampire lord.  I had -4 in protection.  I had
identified ALL the scrolls and potions.  I had +2 snickersnee.  I was
level 13 Samurai with 119 HP's.  My stats were all really good, due to
finding gain ability potions (which I blessed).   I had a unicorn
horn.  I had resistance to cold, poison, and sleep.  I was telepathic,
invisible, and detected invisibility.  Black dragons were conveniently
genocided.  I was ready to deal with anything, right?  Wrong.

Well, after descending the stairs, I met the worst monster of all.
Yep, the collapsing dungeon.  "Aaaargh!"  I say to myself.  So, I said
to myself: "Self, you're going to have to run the recover program."

The levels.0 file was gone.  No recovery is possible.

AAAAAAAAAAAAAAGGGGGGGGGGGGGHHHHHH!!!!!!!!!

Yell.  Scream.  Panic.  Scream some more.  Curse.  Panic again, just to
get it out of the system.  Gibber meaninglessly.  Pound head on keyboard.
Again.  Again.  One last time.  Finish up with a round cursing of all
computer programmers.  Remember that self is a programmer.  Whimper
pitifully.

Upon death, the program rightfully erases the levels.0 file to keep
cheaters from recovering at that point.  However, a collapsing dungeon
is not a typical death.  It should NOT delete the levels files.  At
least, it should ask first.

I'm not playing this game again, until I'm assured that it is stable.
It's just NOT FAIR.  Call me when you find a stable patch.  I'm going
to pout until then.

